<Page title="About SepticSteward: Septic System Guides for Homeowners" description="SepticSteward is a free, plain English guide to septic system care for homeowners: real maintenance intervals, real costs, no jargon.">
  <p>{site.BRAND} is an independent site. {site.author.bio}</p>

  <h2>What this site is</h2>
  <p>Septic neglect is expensive and mostly avoidable: a typical 1,000-gallon tank needs pumping roughly every three to five years depending on household size, and drainfield failures usually trace back to skipped inspections rather than bad luck. We cover tank sizing, pumping intervals, and realistic repair and replacement costs by region, without the scare tactics that pumping companies sometimes lean on.</p>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>Maintenance intervals and design standards come from EPA onsite wastewater treatment guidance and state health department septic codes. Pages are drafted with AI assistance and checked against those codes before publishing, described fully in our <a href="/editorial/">editorial policy</a>. Cost estimates are ranges pulled from multiple regional contractor quotes rather than a single source.</p>

  <h2>How we make money</h2>
  <p>This site is free for homeowners to use. We earn affiliate commissions when readers buy septic treatment products or tools through links here, disclosed in our <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure</a>.</p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>State septic codes and typical costs shift over time. Report an outdated figure through <a href="/contact/">contact</a> and we'll correct and date it.</p>
</Page>
